# Trailing-slash canonicalisation, as a 301.
#
# The asset router already normalises /path -> /path/ but answers 307
# (temporary), which tells Google to keep the slashless URL and not pass
# signals to the real one — that is why 16 of them sat in Search Console as
# "Page with redirect". A 301 consolidates them instead. Nothing on the site
# links to the slashless form any more; these are for old links and typed URLs.
/services/:service/:area   /services/:service/:area/   301
/services/:service         /services/:service/         301
/service-areas/:area       /service-areas/:area/       301
/car-keys/:make            /car-keys/:make/            301

# Top-level pages need their own lines. A /:page placeholder would also swallow
# /robots.txt, /favicon.ico and every asset at the root, so these are
# enumerated. Without them the asset router answers /faq with a 307, which
# tells Google the slashless URL is the real one and not to pass signals on —
# exactly what left /faq and /service-areas sitting in "Page with redirect"
# while the 88 deeper URLs resolved correctly.
/about                     /about/                     301
/contact                   /contact/                   301
/faq                       /faq/                       301
/reviews                   /reviews/                   301
/services                  /services/                  301
/service-areas             /service-areas/             301
/car-keys                  /car-keys/                  301
/how-to-hire-a-locksmith   /how-to-hire-a-locksmith/   301
